   __SS__ee__cc__tt__ii__oo__nn __11__..____II__nn__tt__rr__oo__dd__uu__cc__tt__ii__oo__nn____________ 

   This document covers installation of the OCT system.  Most of
   the document is a tutorial based around building a sample
   class.  This tutorial should help outline the daily care and
   feeding of OCT.  If your site has _m_a_k_e then tracking changes in
   the file can be automated.  

        The  uses several resources from the host.  Normal utilties
   to produce executables from "C" source code are required.  The
   UNIX user of the OCT asks the system to supply _c_p_p (the C
   pre-processor).  Included with the OCT is DECUS's version of _c_p_p
   in case there is none locally (like most AmigaDOS and MS-DOS
   systems).  

        The OCT must somehow find the include files.  Environment
   variables hold the list of directories to search.  Normally one
   more directory must be appended to a list somewhere.
   Alternatively, a script or mmaakkeeffiillee make explicitly specify a
   directory (see man page for _o_o_c ).  Include files from Object C
   Translator don't need to mingle with your systems own files, if
   you don't want.  

        Linking does require searching through libraries.  By
   installing the libraries in //uussrr//lliibb the class libraries can be
   seperate from the systems libraries.  


   11..11.. SSyysstteemm CCoommppoonneennttss      

        A running OCT application is the product of source files,
   interface definitions, and translation programs.  The Object C
   Translator programs include an OCT to "C" source code
   translator, a class interface helper, and a pre-linker utility.
   Your site must provide a K&R version 1 [Kern78] "C" compiler.  

        The interface definition file includes information about
   the class, its superclass, and method return types.  The
   prelinker program arranges for the needed classes to be included
   from the OCT object library.  The output "C" file is then linked
   along with application files and the OCT libraries.  
