   The first two passes are driven by OCT, which calls _c_p_p first.
   The translator then converts class definitions and methods into
   legal "C" code.  The translator uses information in the
   @interface clauses to relate the external classes.  The system's
   "C" compiler runs next.  The prelinker creates a list of classes
   for use by the substrate.  









































