   Before the user application can begin running, the system must
   initialize itself.  Each class will see the "initialize" message
   first, which will most likely be fielded by class OObbjjeecctt as the
   default implementation.  The user's main() function name has
   been changed via a #define in  <<oobbjjcc//oobbjjcc..hh>>..  This allows
   (almost) seamless operation with pre-existing source files, and
   requires nothing special from the run-time environment.  Since
   many microcomputer "C" runtime libraries don't have _atexit(),
   the include file also redirects exit().  This allows the
   substrate to cleanup.  Setting the global (BOOL) msgTrace will
   print out some statistics when the application exits.  


